    Bug 1905616 - Open same-site links with a target attribute on http(s):// content pages in a new tab, if required. r=mkmelin

    We already open same-site links with a target attribute on
    moz-extension:// content pages in a new tab if needed. We do not have
    special code for that, but this is correctly handled by the default
    click handler.

    The default click handler (which I was not able to find), however does
    not handle this correctly for http(s):// content pages. The page is
    opened in the same tab and then goes blank.

    This patch is adding code to check if the requested BrowsingContext
    exists and can be navigated to. If not, the default handler action is
    prevented and we manually open a new tab.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D229753

